# Tests

A test exists when a wrong result would misstate an account, a split, or a movement. Do not write a test whose only assert is that a class was created or that a method was called.

Test pure functions in `domain/` directly. Write a component test only when the screen decides the rule: which categories it offers, which payload it sends, which label it shows.

In this frontend, protect:

- `pesosToCents` rounds to cents and `formatMoney` displays COP.
- An income is a haircut, makeup, or other. An expense is not a haircut.
- A $0 movement is not sent. The payload goes out in cents. An empty note is not sent.
- Status reads as "En recuperación", "Capital recuperado", or "Pérdida del mes".
- December moves forward to January of the next year. January moves back to December of the previous year.

The split, capital recovery, and monthly profit arrive in `IMonthlySummary`. That calculation belongs to the backend. Here, test how it is presented and what is decided before it is sent.

```typescript
it('rounds pesos to cents', () => {
  expect(pesosToCents(10.005)).toBe(1001);
});
```
